"""The curated rows of the coverage matrix: one row per decision or action a competent player takes.

Each row: id, domain, m (the mechanic), src (where the game defines it), tools (MCP tools that read or act on it),
ex (regex over the executor plan_*.rs, test modules cut), mon (regex over the monitor), st (regex over the
strategist's skills and scripts), plan (regex over the plan), imp (high/medium/low/n/a), why (one reason, the
game's numbers where possible), work (smallest closing work), commands (game command classes it maps to),
state/reason (only when the computed state is wrong: the reason says why).

The inventory-driven groups (air and naval missions, diplomatic actions, buildings, operations, agency branches,
laws, doctrine folders, raid categories, project specialisations) are generated from `inv` so a new game version
or a mod shows its new entries as new rows (with NOT HANDLED until a mapping below names their tool).
"""
import re


def R(id, domain, m, src='', tools=(), ex=None, mon=None, st=None, plan=None, imp='medium', why='', work='',
      state=None, reason='', commands=(), proof=None):
    return {'proof': proof, 'id': id, 'domain': domain, 'm': m, 'src': src, 'tools': list(tools), 'ex': ex, 'mon': mon, 'st': st,
            'plan': plan, 'imp': imp, 'why': why, 'work': work, 'state': state, 'reason': reason,
            'commands': list(commands)}


